Part of the fun of Nethack is the random level generation. Other dungeon 
crawls get boring really fast because the player can take advantage of 
monster spawn points, always knowing where a certain potent artifact 
would pop up and eventually following a pattern. Nethack requires more 
skill than learning and following a pattern. As annoying as Gehennom can 
be, at least it's different every time. Except for the special lair 
levels and such. If Nethack didn't have random level generation then I 
would've stopped playing back in 2000.

